Transforming felicity and adversity into the spiritual path / by Jigme Tenpe Nyima","pagenum":"","type":{"key":"/type/toc_item"}},{"level":0,"label":"","title":"Releasing oneself from essential delusion / by Lochen Dharma Shri","pagenum":"","type":{"key":"/type/toc_item"}},{"level":0,"label":"","title":"The illumination of primordial wisdom / by His Holiness Dudjom Rinpoche.","pagenum":"","type":{"key":"/type/toc_item"}}],"isbn_10":["1559391839"],"pagination":"174 p. ;","covers":[786742],"lc_classifications":["BQ7662.6 .G93 2002","BQ7662.6"],"key":"/books/OL3703249M","publish_places":["Ithaca, N.Y"],"contributions":["Jigme Tenpe Nyima. 2002.","Lochen Dharma Shri. 2002.","Bdud-ʼjoms ʼJigs-bral-ye-śes-rdo-rje, 1904- 2002.","Gyatrul, Rinpoche, 1924-","Khandro, Sangye.","Wallace, B. Alan."],"languages":[{"key":"/languages/eng"}],"genres":["Doctrines."],"source_records":["marc:marc_records_scriblio_net/part14.dat:166892894:1428","marc:marc_loc_updates/v38.i33.records.utf8:21890196:1440","bwb:9781559391832","marc:marc_loc_2016/BooksAll.2016.part30.utf8:223061392:1420","marc:marc_columbia/Columbia-extract-20221130-007.mrc:393090751:2957","marc:harvard_bibliographic_metadata/ab.bib.09.20150123.full.mrc:19386760:2171","marc:harvard_bibliographic_metadata/20220215_016.bib.mrc:244820496:3123"],"title":"Meditation, transformation, and dream yoga","lccn":["2003270480"],"number_of_pages":174,"edition_name":"2nd ed.","subjects":["Spiritual life -- Rñiṅ-ma-pa (Sect)","Rñiṅ-ma-pa (Sect) -- Doctrines"],"publish_date":"2002","publish_country":"nyu","by_statement":"by Gyatrul Rinpoche ; translations by Sangye Khandro and B. Alan Wallace.","oclc_numbers":["51394445"],"works":[{"key":"/works/OL18334991W"}],"type":{"key":"/type/edition"},"description":{"type":"/type/text","value":"\"The three traditional Nyingma texts included in this book were selected by Ven. Gyatrul Rinpoche for their relevance to the modern-day spiritual aspirant who must combine and balance quality practice time, work time and rest time in the course of a busy day.\".\n\n\"Guidelines for formal sitting are presented from the Dzogchen perspective in the teachings on quiescence meditation. Practices for bringing the experiences of daily life into the spiritual path are presented in the section on transformation. Finally, the teachings on dream yoga guide the practitioner in the conscious control of the dream state as well as the bardo state at the end of life.\".\n\n\"Complementing each section is a dynamic and practical commentary by Ven. Gyatrul Rinpoche specially tailored to the needs of Western students. The result is an indispensable handbook for practitioners at all levels of experience.\"--BOOK JACKET."},"latest_revision":12,"revision":12,"created":{"type":"/type/datetime","value":"2008-04-01T03:28:50.625462"},"last_modified":{"type":"/type/datetime","value":"2025-09-04T08:45:37.476132"}}}}